<Base lang="en" title="Notes"><article class="prose"><p class="label">Traces</p><h1>Some things need not become a project first.</h1><div class="grid"><section class="card"><div><span class="number">CASE NOTES</span><h3>Case notes</h3><p>On systems, evidence, and the process of being recognized. Public notes retain only redacted facts, timelines, and shareable learning—never personal data, raw evidence, or details that could affect a process.</p></div></section></div><section class="cats"><span class="number">TRACES</span><h3>Cats & everyday life</h3><p>No captions, no story arc — just a small, ordinary photo wall. Click one to see it larger.</p><CatAlbum lang="en" /></section><aside class="note">Case notes and cats have separate rooms here: one asks for accuracy; the other only asks to be remembered well.</aside></article></Base>

<style>
  .cats { margin:56px 0 0; } .cats .number { font:.68rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,monospace; color:var(--rose); } .cats h3 { font-size:1.55rem; font-weight:500; margin:13px 0 6px; } .cats p { color:var(--muted); margin:0; font-size:.92rem; }
</style>
